From: conda-forge nodejs-feedstock <noreply@conda-forge.org>
Date: Mon, 25 Aug 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 7/7] Guard V8's string hasher SIMD path on scalar-only Highway
 targets

Companion to the previous patch. V8 has a second unconditional fixed-width
Highway tag: IsOnly8BitSIMD in string-hasher.cc builds a
hw::FixedTag<uint16_t, 8>, which also needs a 16-byte vector and so also fails
on linux-riscv64, where HWY_SCALAR is the static target:

  shared-inl.h:369:27: error: static assertion failed: Too many lanes
  string-hasher.cc:82:38: error: no matching function for call to
    'Set(hwy::N_SCALAR::FixedTag<short unsigned int, 8>&, uint16_t)'

The other two Highway users in V8, runtime-regexp.cc and unicode.cc, use
ScalableTag and are fine on HWY_SCALAR.

IsOnly8BitSIMD is not a template, so its body is always instantiated and the
"if constexpr" used in json-stringifier.cc would not prevent the error. A
preprocessor guard is required, and HWY_LANES(T) cannot be used in #if because
it expands to a sizeof expression; HWY_MAX_BYTES is a plain integer literal per
target (8 for HWY_SCALAR, >= 16 for everything else), so guard on that instead.

The trailing scalar loop already handles arbitrary lengths and becomes the
whole implementation on such targets.
---
 deps/v8/src/strings/string-hasher.cc | 20 ++++++++++++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 20 insertions(+), 1 deletions(-)

--- a/deps/v8/src/strings/string-hasher.cc
+++ b/deps/v8/src/strings/string-hasher.cc
@@ -76,13 +76,31 @@
 }
 
 bool IsOnly8BitSIMD(const uint16_t* chars, unsigned len) {
+  const uint16_t* end = chars + len;
+// FixedTag<uint16_t, 8> needs a 16-byte vector. Highway falls back to
+// HWY_SCALAR (HWY_MAX_BYTES == 8) whenever neither a native SIMD target nor
+// EMU128 is available, which is the case for riscv64 without the V extension
+// when built with GCC: HWY_RVV is excluded and HWY_BROKEN_EMU128 is set for
+// GCC < 16, leaving HWY_SCALAR as the static target. The tag then fails to
+// compile:
+//
+//   shared-inl.h:369:27: error: static assertion failed: Too many lanes
+//   string-hasher.cc:82:38: error: no matching function for call to
+//     'Set(hwy::N_SCALAR::FixedTag<short unsigned int, 8>&, uint16_t)'
+//
+// Unlike AppendString in json-stringifier.cc this is not a template, so the
+// body is always instantiated and "if constexpr" would not help; and
+// HWY_LANES(T) expands to a sizeof expression, which is not usable in #if.
+// HWY_MAX_BYTES is a plain integer literal per target, so guard on that. The
+// scalar loop below already handles arbitrary lengths and is a complete
+// fallback; targets that do provide 16-byte vectors are unaffected.
+#if HWY_MAX_BYTES >= 16
   namespace hw = hwy::HWY_NAMESPACE;
   hw::FixedTag<uint16_t, 8> tag;
   const size_t stride = hw::Lanes(tag);
   const auto high_byte_mask = hw::Set(tag, static_cast<uint16_t>(0xFF00));
   const auto zero = hw::Zero(tag);
 
-  const uint16_t* end = chars + len;
   while (chars + stride <= end) {
     const auto data = hw::LoadU(tag, chars);
     const auto high_bytes = hw::And(data, high_byte_mask);
@@ -92,6 +110,7 @@
     }
     chars += stride;
   }
+#endif  // HWY_MAX_BYTES >= 16
   // Handle remaining characters.
   while (chars < end) {
     if (*chars > 0xFF) {
